.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-KEY-REPLACE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-key-replace - Replace the team's recording key with a new one signed by your copy of the current key


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings key replace [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace the team's recording key.

.PP
The new key is made and signed here with your ENV vault: only a member who holds a copy of the current key can sign the next one, so machines follow it through the signed chain and never because the server says so. Everyone who can replay gets a copy of the new key, and older recordings stay readable through a link sealed to it. The key and its private halves never leave this computer in plaintext.

.PP
Needs the security permission on the team and an unlocked ENV vault (\fBpb env unlock\fR).

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	must be \fBREPLACE RECORDING KEY <team>\fR

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for replace

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team whose key to replace; defaults to the active workspace


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings-key(1)\fP
